## Checkpoint-interface audit

`host/kevin_jtag_cli.py` provides `infer`, `program`, and `debug`.  `debug`
decodes one 40-byte `DBG1` snapshot (sequencer state, layer/position, busy
flags, embedding component, and one LayerNorm lane).  It has no command,
capture protocol, or CSR iteration that can emit the twelve required
block-0 token-step tensors.  The existing client therefore cannot create a
`tinystories-1m-board-checkpoint-receipt-v1` without a separately scoped,
board-compatible debug-interface implementation.
